Okay. First of all, you're fine with your equipment! (Though take off
your ring of levitation ;-)  And be carefull, nevertheless...

Since you're unburdened you could jump (if you have the boots or the
spell) around the riders if you like.

Don't let the Riders come close to you! And with your multifire arrows
they won't come close. Pestilence and Famine can be killed by the wand
of death (Death naturally won't be affected); but since the wand of
death may miss I think with your arrows are still the primary choice.
(If you have a bouncing wall and one of the two susceptible Riders in
between you may as well try to zap the wand.

Don't ever zap a wand of teleportation in the direction of any Rider or
any Rider corpse (they would instantly revive adjacent to you)!

The so called player characters are very good equiped with armor and
some creature may carry an artifact weapon, even one with beheading
properties.

You already know about the tough priests from Moloch's Sanctum, so you
know what to expect about them. Zap away a row of them if they happen
to line up in your way. The ants that they occasionally summon can act
as your living shield; use it wisely.

If you reached the wrong altar and you feel too weak to pass two of the
Riders again you may as well wish for a helm of opposite alignment to
convert to chaos or lawful; if it's the wrong alignment you need some
means to uncurse the auto-cursing helm and can retry changing alignment
until you match the altar alignment and as long as you have can uncurse
the helm. But you seem good enough prepared to visit all three altars.
:-)

Good luck for the final step!

